00:01:09.776 --> 00:01:13.776
When a tenant gives notice, start here:
the Checkout button on their page.

2
00:01:14.926 --> 00:01:21.926
One page replaces the paper form — and the
box on the right is the live refund maths.

3
00:01:23.071 --> 00:01:28.854
The deposit held and any unpaid rent are
pulled in automatically. No hunting

4
00:01:28.854 --> 00:01:30.354
through ledgers.

5
00:01:30.354 --> 00:01:36.491
Walk the unit, record what you find.
Damage here will become a deduction in a

6
00:01:36.491 --> 00:01:37.991
moment.

7
00:01:42.846 --> 00:01:49.846
Add each deduction with its own line and
amount — and watch the refund update live.

8
00:01:49.861 --> 00:01:56.861
Itemised beats a lump sum: the tenant can
see exactly how the number was reached.

9
00:01:56.867 --> 00:02:03.367
Keys, utility handover, and how the refund
goes out — all on the record.

10
00:02:06.012 --> 00:02:11.512
Save as you go. Nothing is final yet — the
checkout stays in progress.

11
00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:18.362
Finalising does the close-out in one
stroke: tenant vacated, unit vacant,

12
00:02:18.362 --> 00:02:19.862
deposit settled.

13
00:02:19.862 --> 00:02:24.634
Out comes the statement PDF, ready for
both signatures.

14
00:02:24.649 --> 00:02:30.649
The record locks read-only. The goodbye is
clean, documented, and defensible.

15
00:02:30.663 --> 00:02:35.553
That's the full loop — from first tenant
to final refund. Browse the rest any time

16
